cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Syracuse/Collatz research and formalization artifacts, please cite Ta-Yoshua Lubuimi."
title: "Syracuse Offset, Valuation Cylinders, and Terminal-Residue Energy"
authors:
  - family-names: "Lubuimi"
    given-names: "Ta-Yoshua"
date-released: 2026-11-10
version: "0.2.0"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Research and Lean formalization artifacts for accelerated Syracuse dynamics.
  The repository records exact affine offset and signed-margin identities,
  the classical initial valuation-one cylinder classification, independently
  derived and formally verified by the author on multiple exact CI snapshots,
  the finite exact valuation-word cylinder classification, and the terminal-residue collision-energy and finite
  Markov-matrix constructions. The citation does not imply a proof of the
  global Collatz conjecture; the broader finite-word and collision-energy
  extensions remain separate Lean formalization targets.
repository-code: "https://github.com/s4ztz4bnf6-maker/Lubuimi"
url: "https://github.com/s4ztz4bnf6-maker/Lubuimi"
keywords:
  - "Collatz conjecture"
  - "Syracuse dynamics"
  - "2-adic valuation"
  - "valuation cylinders"
  - "affine offset identity"
  - "terminal residue"
  - "collision energy"
  - "Lean 4"
